Document the saved-session search, and how to work on it

docs/session-search.md: the *how* for the search added in fdba524 - the
prefix rule, what is matched (name, HostName, SessionComment), why a
leading / is free, what the user sees, the per-session cache and where it
is invalidated, the PUTTY_SESS_SEARCH_DEBUG trace, how to drive the dialog
from osascript when no human is available (including the 5-tab route to
the box and the PuTTY-bin gotcha), and what is deliberately left out.

Also: a row for it in the README documentation index, a pointer from
README 9b, a row in the CHANGES-FROM-UPSTREAM new-files table, and a note
in PLAN 4j about where the docs ended up.
